IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`
IMPORT `ssc7-12zd`

-- Tests for Part 12ZD (ss 171ZZ6-171ZZ15).  Every expected value is written beside its assertion from the
-- text of the Act (src:4017-4129), before the run, and is never copied from the code's output.
-- Figures that regulations or other Acts supply (the lower earnings limit, the prescribed rate and number of
-- weeks, the day s 63(3) WRA 2012 comes fully into force) are ARBITRARY TEST INPUTS here, not law.
-- Calendar facts used: 1 January 2026 is a Thursday, so 3 January 2026 is a Saturday and 4 January a Sunday.

§ `Tests for Part 12ZD`

§§ `Fixtures`

`s 171ZZ6 test person` MEANS Person WITH
    `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1990
    `sex` IS Woman
    `marital status` IS `married`
    `date of attaining pensionable age` IS Date 1 1 2057

GIVEN began IS A DATE
      ended IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH AN Employment
`s 171ZZ6 test employment` MEANS Employment WITH
    `the employee` IS `s 171ZZ6 test person`
    `the kind of employer` IS `a company or other body corporate`
    `the employment began on` IS began
    `the employment ended on` IS ended
    `held under a contract of service` IS TRUE
    `held in an office` IS FALSE
    `carried on in Great Britain` IS TRUE

-- A child born alive who died on the given day.
GIVEN died IS A DATE
GIVETH A `s 171ZZ6 the child who died`
`s 171ZZ6 test child who died on` MEANS `s 171ZZ6 the child who died` WITH
    `born dead` IS FALSE
    `weeks of pregnancy when labour began` IS 40
    `the day the child was born` IS Date 1 6 2020
    `the day the child died` IS JUST died

-- A child stillborn on the given day after the given weeks of pregnancy.
GIVEN weeks IS A NUMBER
      born IS A DATE
GIVETH A `s 171ZZ6 the child who died`
`s 171ZZ6 test child stillborn` MEANS `s 171ZZ6 the child who died` WITH
    `born dead` IS TRUE
    `weeks of pregnancy when labour began` IS weeks
    `the day the child was born` IS born
    `the day the child died` IS NOTHING

GIVEN child IS A `s 171ZZ6 the child who died`
      emp IS AN Employment
      weeks IS A NUMBER
      earnings IS A NUMBER
      entitledToBe IS A BOOLEAN
      relationship IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 171ZZ6(2) the person's case`
`s 171ZZ6 test case` MEANS `s 171ZZ6(2) the person's case` WITH
    `the child who died` IS child
    `the employment` IS emp
    `weeks of continuous employment ending with the relevant week` IS weeks
    `normal weekly earnings in pounds for the 8 weeks ending with the relevant week` IS earnings
    `at the end of the relevant week the person was entitled to be in that employment` IS entitledToBe
    `the person satisfies the prescribed conditions as to relationship with the child who died` IS relationship

-- The child died on Saturday 10 January 2026; the relevant week is Sunday 28 December 2025 to Saturday 3 January 2026.
`s 171ZZ6 test death` MEANS Date 10 1 2026
`s 171ZZ6 test base case` MEANS `s 171ZZ6 test case` (`s 171ZZ6 test child who died on` `s 171ZZ6 test death`) (`s 171ZZ6 test employment` (Date 1 1 2025) NOTHING) 52 150 TRUE TRUE
-- An arbitrary test lower earnings limit of 100 pounds a week, and an arbitrary day for s 63(3) WRA 2012 long past.
`s 171ZZ6 test LEL` MEANS 100
`s 171ZZ6 test WRA day past` MEANS Date 1 1 2020
`s 171ZZ6 test WRA day future` MEANS Date 1 1 2030

§§ `s 171ZZ6(5) the relevant week`

`s 171ZZ6 test week` MEANS GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE YIELD Period WITH `the first day` IS a, `the last day` IS b

-- Death on Saturday 10 Jan 2026: its week is Sun 4 - Sat 10 Jan; the week before is Sun 28 Dec 2025 - Sat 3 Jan 2026.
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ6(5) the relevant week` (Date 10 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 28 12 2025, `the last day` IS Date 3 1 2026)
-- Death on Sunday 4 Jan 2026: its week is Sun 4 - Sat 10 Jan; the week before is the same one, 28 Dec - 3 Jan.
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ6(5) the relevant week` (Date 4 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 28 12 2025, `the last day` IS Date 3 1 2026)
-- Death on Saturday 3 Jan 2026: its week is Sun 28 Dec - Sat 3 Jan; the week before is Sun 21 - Sat 27 Dec 2025.
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ6(5) the relevant week` (Date 3 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 21 12 2025, `the last day` IS Date 27 12 2025)
-- Regulations prescribe another period: s 171ZZ14(5) says "such other period as may be prescribed", so not covered.
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ6(5) the relevant week` (Date 10 1 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ6(5) the last day of the relevant week` (Date 10 1 2026) EQUALS Date 3 1 2026
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ6(5) the last day of the relevant week` (Date 4 1 2026) EQUALS Date 3 1 2026
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ6(5) the last day of the relevant week` (Date 3 1 2026) EQUALS Date 27 12 2025

§§ `s 171ZZ6(7) paragraph (c) omitted`

-- A child who dies "before the day": the day before is before, the day itself is not.
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ6(7) paragraph (c) of subsection (2) is omitted` (Date 31 12 2025) (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ6(7) paragraph (c) of subsection (2) is omitted` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ6(7) paragraph (c) of subsection (2) is omitted` (Date 2 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 171ZZ6(2)(b) to (e), one paragraph at a time`

-- (b) "at least 26 weeks": 25 is short, 26 and 27 suffice.
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ6(2)(b) the person has been in employment for at least 26 weeks` 25 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ6(2)(b) the person has been in employment for at least 26 weeks` 26 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ6(2)(b) the person has been in employment for at least 26 weeks` 27 EQUALS TRUE
-- (c) entitled to be in the employment; where (7) omits the paragraph it is taken as satisfied.
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ6(2)(c) the person was entitled to be in that employment` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ6(2)(c) the person was entitled to be in that employment` FALSE NOTHING EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ6(2)(c) the person was entitled to be in that employment` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ6(2)(c) the person was entitled to be in that employment` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
-- (d) "not less than" the lower earnings limit (here the test input 100): 99.99 is less, 100 and 100.01 are not.
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ6(2)(d) the normal weekly earnings are not less than the lower earnings limit` 99.99 100 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ6(2)(d) the normal weekly earnings are not less than the lower earnings limit` 100 100 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ6(2)(d) the normal weekly earnings are not less than the lower earnings limit` 100.01 100 EQUALS TRUE
-- (e) in the employment from the end of the relevant week (Sat 3 Jan 2026) to the day of death (Sat 10 Jan 2026).
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ6(2)(e) the person has been in the employment from the end of the relevant week to the day the child dies` (`s 171ZZ6 test employment` (Date 1 1 2025) NOTHING) (Date 3 1 2026) (Date 10 1 2026) EQUALS TRUE
-- ended the day before the death: not "ending with the day on which the child dies"
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ6(2)(e) the person has been in the employment from the end of the relevant week to the day the child dies` (`s 171ZZ6 test employment` (Date 1 1 2025) (JUST (Date 9 1 2026))) (Date 3 1 2026) (Date 10 1 2026) EQUALS FALSE
-- ended on the day of death: it lasts to the day
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ6(2)(e) the person has been in the employment from the end of the relevant week to the day the child dies` (`s 171ZZ6 test employment` (Date 1 1 2025) (JUST (Date 10 1 2026))) (Date 3 1 2026) (Date 10 1 2026) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ6(2)(e) the person has been in the employment from the end of the relevant week to the day the child dies` (`s 171ZZ6 test employment` (Date 1 1 2025) (JUST (Date 11 1 2026))) (Date 3 1 2026) (Date 10 1 2026) EQUALS TRUE
-- began the day after the end of the relevant week: not "beginning with the end of the relevant week"
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ6(2)(e) the person has been in the employment from the end of the relevant week to the day the child dies` (`s 171ZZ6 test employment` (Date 4 1 2026) NOTHING) (Date 3 1 2026) (Date 10 1 2026) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ6(2)(e) the person has been in the employment from the end of the relevant week to the day the child dies` (`s 171ZZ6 test employment` (Date 3 1 2026) NOTHING) (Date 3 1 2026) (Date 10 1 2026) EQUALS TRUE

§§ `s 171ZZ6(3) bereaved parent`

-- relationship conditions met and the dead child under 18: a bereaved parent
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ6(3) the employee is a bereaved parent` (`s 171ZZ6 test child who died on` (Date 10 1 2026)) (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- relationship conditions not met: "if the employee satisfies" fails (reading (a))
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ6(3) the employee is a bereaved parent` (`s 171ZZ6 test child who died on` (Date 10 1 2026)) (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the person who died was not under 18, so not a "child" (s 171ZZ14(1) "means")
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ6(3) the employee is a bereaved parent` (`s 171ZZ6 test child who died on` (Date 10 1 2026)) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 173(a) does not answer: not covered
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ6(3) the employee is a bereaved parent` (`s 171ZZ6 test child who died on` (Date 10 1 2026)) NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- stillborn after more than 24 weeks counts as a child (s 171ZZ15(a)); the K2 input is not read
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ6(3) the employee is a bereaved parent` (`s 171ZZ6 test child stillborn` 30 (Date 10 1 2026)) NOTHING TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- stillborn at exactly 24 weeks: "include" does not close the list, so not covered
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ6(3) the employee is a bereaved parent` (`s 171ZZ6 test child stillborn` 24 (Date 10 1 2026)) NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 171ZZ6(2)(a), a bereaved parent`

-- (2)(a) with (3): a bereaved parent is an employee who satisfies the prescribed conditions as to relationship with a child who has died; the person who died must be a "child" (under 18, s 173(a))
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ6(2)(a) the person is a bereaved parent` `s 171ZZ6 test base case` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ6(2)(a) the person is a bereaved parent` `s 171ZZ6 test base case` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ6(2)(a) the person is a bereaved parent` `s 171ZZ6 test base case` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 171ZZ6(2) and (1), the whole entitlement`

-- all five paragraphs satisfied (death 10 Jan 2026; earnings 150 against the test limit 100; 52 weeks)
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ6(1) the person is entitled to statutory parental bereavement pay` `s 171ZZ6 test base case` (JUST TRUE) `s 171ZZ6 test LEL` `s 171ZZ6 test WRA day past` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ6(2) the person satisfies the conditions` `s 171ZZ6 test base case` (JUST TRUE) `s 171ZZ6 test LEL` `s 171ZZ6 test WRA day past` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (a) fails alone: relationship conditions not met
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ6(1) the person is entitled to statutory parental bereavement pay` (`s 171ZZ6 test case` (`s 171ZZ6 test child who died on` `s 171ZZ6 test death`) (`s 171ZZ6 test employment` (Date 1 1 2025) NOTHING) 52 150 TRUE FALSE) (JUST TRUE) `s 171ZZ6 test LEL` `s 171ZZ6 test WRA day past` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (b) fails alone: 25 weeks
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ6(1) the person is entitled to statutory parental bereavement pay` (`s 171ZZ6 test case` (`s 171ZZ6 test child who died on` `s 171ZZ6 test death`) (`s 171ZZ6 test employment` (Date 1 1 2025) NOTHING) 25 150 TRUE TRUE) (JUST TRUE) `s 171ZZ6 test LEL` `s 171ZZ6 test WRA day past` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (b) at the boundary: 26 weeks
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ6(1) the person is entitled to statutory parental bereavement pay` (`s 171ZZ6 test case` (`s 171ZZ6 test child who died on` `s 171ZZ6 test death`) (`s 171ZZ6 test employment` (Date 1 1 2025) NOTHING) 26 150 TRUE TRUE) (JUST TRUE) `s 171ZZ6 test LEL` `s 171ZZ6 test WRA day past` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (c) fails alone, death after the WRA day: not entitled to be in the employment at the end of the relevant week
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ6(1) the person is entitled to statutory parental bereavement pay` (`s 171ZZ6 test case` (`s 171ZZ6 test child who died on` `s 171ZZ6 test death`) (`s 171ZZ6 test employment` (Date 1 1 2025) NOTHING) 52 150 FALSE TRUE) (JUST TRUE) `s 171ZZ6 test LEL` `s 171ZZ6 test WRA day past` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (c) same facts, but the child died before the WRA day: paragraph (c) is omitted (s 171ZZ6(7)), so entitled
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ6(1) the person is entitled to statutory parental bereavement pay` (`s 171ZZ6 test case` (`s 171ZZ6 test child who died on` `s 171ZZ6 test death`) (`s 171ZZ6 test employment` (Date 1 1 2025) NOTHING) 52 150 FALSE TRUE) (JUST TRUE) `s 171ZZ6 test LEL` `s 171ZZ6 test WRA day future` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (d) fails alone: 99.99 against 100
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ6(1) the person is entitled to statutory parental bereavement pay` (`s 171ZZ6 test case` (`s 171ZZ6 test child who died on` `s 171ZZ6 test death`) (`s 171ZZ6 test employment` (Date 1 1 2025) NOTHING) 52 99.99 TRUE TRUE) (JUST TRUE) `s 171ZZ6 test LEL` `s 171ZZ6 test WRA day past` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (d) at the boundary: exactly 100
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ6(1) the person is entitled to statutory parental bereavement pay` (`s 171ZZ6 test case` (`s 171ZZ6 test child who died on` `s 171ZZ6 test death`) (`s 171ZZ6 test employment` (Date 1 1 2025) NOTHING) 52 100 TRUE TRUE) (JUST TRUE) `s 171ZZ6 test LEL` `s 171ZZ6 test WRA day past` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (e) fails alone: the employment ended the day before the death
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ6(1) the person is entitled to statutory parental bereavement pay` (`s 171ZZ6 test case` (`s 171ZZ6 test child who died on` `s 171ZZ6 test death`) (`s 171ZZ6 test employment` (Date 1 1 2025) (JUST (Date 9 1 2026))) 52 150 TRUE TRUE) (JUST TRUE) `s 171ZZ6 test LEL` `s 171ZZ6 test WRA day past` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (a) not covered (s 173(a) gives no answer) and every other paragraph satisfied: not covered
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ6(1) the person is entitled to statutory parental bereavement pay` `s 171ZZ6 test base case` NOTHING `s 171ZZ6 test LEL` `s 171ZZ6 test WRA day past` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (a) not covered but paragraph (b) fails: a failed paragraph already makes it no
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ6(1) the person is entitled to statutory parental bereavement pay` (`s 171ZZ6 test case` (`s 171ZZ6 test child who died on` `s 171ZZ6 test death`) (`s 171ZZ6 test employment` (Date 1 1 2025) NOTHING) 25 150 TRUE TRUE) NOTHING `s 171ZZ6 test LEL` `s 171ZZ6 test WRA day past` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- regulations under s 171ZZ7(4) modify or disapply a condition: the text alone cannot answer
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ6(1) the person is entitled to statutory parental bereavement pay` `s 171ZZ6 test base case` (JUST TRUE) `s 171ZZ6 test LEL` `s 171ZZ6 test WRA day past` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- a stillborn child after 30 weeks: the day taken as the day of death is the birth day (Sat 10 Jan 2026), same relevant week
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ6(1) the person is entitled to statutory parental bereavement pay` (`s 171ZZ6 test case` (`s 171ZZ6 test child stillborn` 30 (Date 10 1 2026)) (`s 171ZZ6 test employment` (Date 1 1 2025) NOTHING) 52 150 TRUE TRUE) NOTHING `s 171ZZ6 test LEL` `s 171ZZ6 test WRA day past` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no day of death given for a child born alive: not covered
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ6(1) the person is entitled to statutory parental bereavement pay` (`s 171ZZ6 test case` (`s 171ZZ6 test child stillborn` 24 (Date 10 1 2026)) (`s 171ZZ6 test employment` (Date 1 1 2025) NOTHING) 52 150 TRUE TRUE) NOTHING `s 171ZZ6 test LEL` `s 171ZZ6 test WRA day past` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 171ZZ6(6) more than one child`

#ASSERT `s 171ZZ6(6) the number of children in respect of whom the person is entitled` (LIST JUST TRUE, JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST 2
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ6(6) the number of children in respect of whom the person is entitled` (LIST JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST 1
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ6(6) the number of children in respect of whom the person is entitled` (LIST JUST TRUE, NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ6(6) the number of children in respect of whom the person is entitled` (LIST JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST 1

§§ `s 171ZZ7 notice`

#ASSERT `s 171ZZ7(1) the person is entitled to payments for the weeks` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no notice: "only if the person gives notice", whatever s 171ZZ6(1) says
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ7(1) the person is entitled to payments for the weeks` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ7(1) the person is entitled to payments for the weeks` NOTHING FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- notice given but s 171ZZ6(1) not covered / no
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ7(1) the person is entitled to payments for the weeks` NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ7(1) the person is entitled to payments for the weeks` (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (3) writing is required only if the payer asks
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ7(3) the notice satisfies the requirement as to writing` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ7(3) the notice satisfies the requirement as to writing` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ7(3) the notice satisfies the requirement as to writing` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ7(3) the notice satisfies the requirement as to writing` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `s 171ZZ8 liability`

#ASSERT `s 171ZZ8(1) the person is liable to make payments of statutory parental bereavement pay` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not an employer in the s 171ZZ6(2)(b), (e) sense: s 171ZZ8(3) lets regulations make the Commissioners liable, so not covered
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ8(1) the person is liable to make payments of statutory parental bereavement pay` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the duty as a regulative rule: the liable person pays 100 and the duty is FULFILLED (no time limit in the text)
#TRACE `s 171ZZ8(1) the duty to make the payments` 100 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 171ZZ8 the person liable to make the payments` DOES `s 171ZZ8 makes a payment of statutory parental bereavement pay` 100 AT 1

§§ `s 171ZZ9 rate and period of pay`

#ASSERT `s 171ZZ9(1) the weekly rate of statutory parental bereavement pay in pounds` (JUST 100) EQUALS JUST 100
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ9(1) the weekly rate of statutory parental bereavement pay in pounds` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2): rate 100; 2 weeks of a prescribed 2 within the qualifying period
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ9(2) the pay payable for the weeks chosen in pounds` 100 2 2 TRUE EQUALS JUST 200
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ9(2) the pay payable for the weeks chosen in pounds` 100 1 2 TRUE EQUALS JUST 100
-- more weeks than the prescribed number: outside the grant
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ9(2) the pay payable for the weeks chosen in pounds` 100 3 2 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- weeks not within the qualifying period: outside the grant
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ9(2) the pay payable for the weeks chosen in pounds` 100 2 2 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3) "not less than two"
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ9(3) the prescribed number of weeks is allowed` 1 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ9(3) the prescribed number of weeks is allowed` 2 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ9(3) the prescribed number of weeks is allowed` 3 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (5) "at least 56 days beginning with the date of the child's death": 1 Jan to 25 Feb 2026 is 31 + 25 = 56 days
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ9(5) the qualifying period is allowed` (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2026, `the last day` IS Date 25 2 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ9(5) the qualifying period is allowed` (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2026, `the last day` IS Date 24 2 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ9(5) the qualifying period is allowed` (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2026, `the last day` IS Date 31 3 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not beginning with the date of the death
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ9(5) the qualifying period is allowed` (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 2 1 2026, `the last day` IS Date 31 3 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (6), (7)
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ9(6) the person is liable to pay for the statutory pay week` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ9(6) the person is liable to pay for the statutory pay week` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ9(7) the person is liable to pay for the statutory pay week whether or not the contract existed before` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ9(7) the person is liable to pay for the statutory pay week whether or not the contract existed before` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ9(7) the person is liable to pay for the statutory pay week whether or not the contract existed before` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ9(7) the person is liable to pay for the statutory pay week whether or not the contract existed before` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (8)
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ9(8) the pay is payable for the statutory pay week` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ9(8) the pay is payable for the statutory pay week` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ9(8) the pay is payable for the statutory pay week` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ9(8) the pay is payable for the statutory pay week` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (10) one seventh of the weekly rate
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ9(10) the daily rate in pounds` 70 EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ9(10) the daily rate in pounds` 7 EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ9(10) the daily rate in pounds` 0 EQUALS 0
-- (11) a week is any period of seven days, both ends counted
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ9(11) the period is a week` (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2026, `the last day` IS Date 7 1 2026) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ9(11) the period is a week` (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2026, `the last day` IS Date 6 1 2026) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ9(11) the period is a week` (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2026, `the last day` IS Date 8 1 2026) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ9(11) the period is a statutory pay week` (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2026, `the last day` IS Date 7 1 2026) TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ9(11) the period is a statutory pay week` (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2026, `the last day` IS Date 8 1 2026) TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ9(11) the period is a statutory pay week` (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2026, `the last day` IS Date 7 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ9(11) the week convention` EQUALS `any period of 7 days`

§§ `s 171ZZ10 contracting out`

#ASSERT `s 171ZZ10(1) the agreement is void to that extent` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ10(1) the agreement is void to that extent` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ10(1) the agreement is void to that extent` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ10(1) the agreement is void to that extent` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ10(2) the agreement authorising deductions is not void by virtue of subsection (1)(a)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ10(2) the agreement authorising deductions is not void by virtue of subsection (1)(a)` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ10(2) the agreement authorising deductions is not void by virtue of subsection (1)(a)` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 171ZZ11 contractual remuneration`

#ASSERT `s 171ZZ11(1) the entitlement affects the person's right to contractual remuneration` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ11(1) the entitlement affects the person's right to contractual remuneration` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2)(a) liability 300 less remuneration paid 100 leaves 200; paid 300 or more leaves nothing
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ11(2)(a) the liability to pay statutory parental bereavement pay that remains` 300 100 EQUALS 200
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ11(2)(a) the liability to pay statutory parental bereavement pay that remains` 300 300 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ11(2)(a) the liability to pay statutory parental bereavement pay that remains` 300 400 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ11(2)(a) the liability to pay statutory parental bereavement pay that remains` 300 0 EQUALS 300
-- (2)(b) the same the other way round
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ11(2)(b) the liability to pay contractual remuneration that remains` 500 200 EQUALS 300
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ11(2)(b) the liability to pay contractual remuneration that remains` 500 500 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ11(2)(b) the liability to pay contractual remuneration that remains` 500 600 EQUALS 0

§§ `s 171ZZ12 Crown employment`

-- the same answer whoever the employer is
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ12 the provisions of this Part apply to the person` `the Crown` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ12 the provisions of this Part apply to the person` `a company or other body corporate` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ12 the provisions of this Part apply to the person` `an individual` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ12 the provisions of this Part apply to the person` `a government department, public authority or other body of persons` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ12 the provisions of this Part apply to the person` `the Crown` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ12 the provisions of this Part apply to the person` `the Crown` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 171ZZ13 special classes`

#ASSERT `s 171ZZ13(1) regulations may modify this Part in its application to the person` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ13(1) regulations may modify this Part in its application to the person` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (c) needs both "prescribed employment" and continental shelf operations
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ13(1) regulations may modify this Part in its application to the person` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ13(1) regulations may modify this Part in its application to the person` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ13(1) regulations may modify this Part in its application to the person` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ13(1) regulations may modify this Part in its application to the person` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 171ZZ14 supplementary`

-- (1) "child": a person under 18, or (s 171ZZ15) a child stillborn after 24 weeks
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ14(1) the person who died was a child` FALSE 40 (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ14(1) the person who died was a child` FALSE 40 (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ14(1) the person who died was a child` FALSE 40 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ14(1) the person who died was a child` TRUE 25 NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ14(1) the person who died was a child` TRUE 24 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1) "employer": liable under s 6, or would be but for 6(1)(b) or the employee's being under 16
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ14(1) the person is the employer of the employee` TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ14(1) the person is the employer of the employee` FALSE TRUE FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ14(1) the person is the employer of the employee` FALSE FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- would be liable but for age, but s 173(a) says the employee is not under 16: no
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ14(1) the person is the employer of the employee` FALSE FALSE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- would be liable but for age, and s 173(a) does not answer: not covered
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ14(1) the person is the employer of the employee` FALSE FALSE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- none of the limbs: "means a person who ..." says no
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ14(1) the person is the employer of the employee` FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ14(1) the person is the employer of the employee` FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (1) "modifications includes additions, omissions and amendments"
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ14(1) the change is a modification` `s 171ZZ14(1) an addition` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ14(1) the change is a modification` `s 171ZZ14(1) an omission` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ14(1) the change is a modification` `s 171ZZ14(1) an amendment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ14(1) the change is a modification` `s 171ZZ14(1) another kind of change` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1) "prescribed means prescribed by regulations"
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ14(1) the matter is prescribed` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ14(1) the matter is prescribed` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2) "employee": in Great Britain, under a contract of service or in an office, with earnings
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ14(2) the person is an employee` (`s 171ZZ6 test employment` (Date 1 1 2025) NOTHING) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ14(2) the person is an employee` (`s 171ZZ6 test employment` (Date 1 1 2025) NOTHING) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ14(2) the person is an employee` (Employment WITH `the employee` IS `s 171ZZ6 test person`, `the kind of employer` IS `the Crown`, `the employment began on` IS Date 1 1 2025, `the employment ended on` IS NOTHING, `held under a contract of service` IS FALSE, `held in an office` IS TRUE, `carried on in Great Britain` IS TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ14(2) the person is an employee` (Employment WITH `the employee` IS `s 171ZZ6 test person`, `the kind of employer` IS `the Crown`, `the employment began on` IS Date 1 1 2025, `the employment ended on` IS NOTHING, `held under a contract of service` IS FALSE, `held in an office` IS FALSE, `carried on in Great Britain` IS TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ14(2) the person is an employee` (Employment WITH `the employee` IS `s 171ZZ6 test person`, `the kind of employer` IS `the Crown`, `the employment began on` IS Date 1 1 2025, `the employment ended on` IS NOTHING, `held under a contract of service` IS TRUE, `held in an office` IS FALSE, `carried on in Great Britain` IS FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (5) week: Sunday-start unless regulations prescribe otherwise.  Wed 7 Jan 2026's week begins Sunday 4 Jan 2026.
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ14(5) the week convention` EQUALS `a period of 7 days beginning with Sunday or another prescribed period`
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ14(5) the first day of the week containing the day` (Date 7 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 4 1 2026)
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ14(5) the first day of the week containing the day` (Date 4 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 4 1 2026)
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ14(5) the first day of the week containing the day` (Date 3 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 28 12 2025)
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ14(5) the first day of the week containing the day` (Date 7 1 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (6) average weekly earnings: 800 over 8 weeks is 100; a prescribed other calculation, or no weeks, is not covered
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ14(6) the person's normal weekly earnings in pounds` 800 8 FALSE EQUALS JUST 100
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ14(6) the person's normal weekly earnings in pounds` 800 8 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ14(6) the person's normal weekly earnings in pounds` 800 0 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 171ZZ15 stillbirths`

-- (a) "after twenty-four weeks": 24 weeks and 1 day is after (24 + 1/7 weeks); 24 weeks exactly is not; "include" leaves the rest uncovered
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ15(a) the child stillborn after twenty-four weeks of pregnancy is a child` TRUE (24 PLUS 1 DIVIDED BY 7) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ15(a) the child stillborn after twenty-four weeks of pregnancy is a child` TRUE 24 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ15(a) the child stillborn after twenty-four weeks of pregnancy is a child` TRUE 23 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ15(a) the child stillborn after twenty-four weeks of pregnancy is a child` FALSE 40 EQUALS NOTHING
-- (b) the death of a stillborn child is read as its birth
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ15(b) the day taken as the day the child dies` TRUE (Date 10 1 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST (Date 10 1 2026)
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ15(b) the day taken as the day the child dies` FALSE (Date 1 6 2020) (JUST (Date 10 1 2026)) EQUALS JUST (Date 10 1 2026)
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ15(b) the day taken as the day the child dies` FALSE (Date 1 6 2020) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
